  "description": "VOJHOR crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P c c n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C82 H82 Cl2 Cu4 La4 N18 O36 2+,2(Cl1 O4 1-),2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, La1 (La) has 9 O neighbors; La2 (La) has 8 O neighbors; Cu1 (Cu) has 3 O neighbors; Cu2 (Cu) has 2 O neighbors; La1D (La) has 9 O neighbors; La2D (La) has 8 O neighbors; Cu2D (Cu) has 2 O neighbors; Cu1D (Cu) has 3 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 11 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.017-4.142 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.56-116.62°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Cu4La4(L)8(LH)8(ClO4)2(NO3)2(OH)4(CH3O)2](ClO4)2·2H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
